  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Brethren, if a man be overtaken in a fault, ye which are spiritual, restore such an one in the spirit of meekness; considering thyself, lest thou also be tempted.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Bear ye one another’s burdens, and so fulfil the law of Christ.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For if a man think himself to be something, when he is nothing, he deceiveth himself.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "But let every man prove his own work, and then shall he have rejoicing in himself alone, and not in another.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "For every man shall bear his own burden.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Let him that is taught in the word communicate unto him that teacheth in all good things.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Be not deceived; God is not mocked: for whatsoever a man soweth, that shall he also reap.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "For he that soweth to his flesh shall of the flesh reap corruption; but he that soweth to the Spirit shall of the Spirit reap life everlasting.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "And let us not be weary in well doing: for in due season we shall reap, if we faint not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "As we have therefore opportunity, let us do good unto all men, especially unto them who are of the household of faith.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Ye see how large a letter I have written unto you with mine own hand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "As many as desire to make a fair shew in the flesh, they constrain you to be circumcised; only lest they should suffer persecution for the cross of Christ.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "For neither they themselves who are circumcised keep the law; but desire to have you circumcised, that they may glory in your flesh.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "But God forbid that I should glory, save in the cross of our Lord Jesus Christ, by whom the world is crucified unto me, and I unto the world.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "For in Christ Jesus neither circumcision availeth any thing, nor uncircumcision, but a new creature.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "And as many as walk according to this rule, peace be on them, and mercy, and upon the Israel of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "From henceforth let no man trouble me: for I bear in my body the marks of the Lord Jesus.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:6:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Brethren, the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Amen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 6:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:6:18"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
